From 8eb86da5e381012d081848788901f2e679a8370c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:26:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(coreelec): switch refresh rates and follow hotplug on
 DRM displays

On CoreELEC Amlogic-no the window shows frames through DRM, where the
driver ignores /sys/class/display mode writes, so auto frame rate did
nothing and an unplugged TV froze the picture for good (a page flip that
never completed kept both buffers locked).

- Auto frame rate on DRM: SetFrameRate's choice (now ChooseModeSwitch,
  shared with the framebuffer path) goes to the GBM window, which switches
  to the same-size mode on the next frame. 23.976 Hz and friends use the
  connector's FRAC_RATE_POLICY property. Close restores the mode and
  1000/1001 state the display had, for Kodi.
- Hotplug: the window re-reads the connector once a second. It stops
  showing frames while the TV is gone and, when one is back, shows the
  mode of the window's size closest to the last one (ChooseOutputMode).
  A flip that does not complete turns scanout off and starts over.
- The flip-done flag lives in the window, not on the stack, so a late
  event cannot write into a finished call.
